.TH "ZLUKS" "8" "2026-10-19" "" "ZFSBootMenu"
.SH NAME
zluks \- manage LUKS volumes from ZFSBootMenu
.SH SYNOPSIS
.sp
\fBzluks\fP [\fBunlock\fP]
.sp
\fBzluks\fP \fBopen\fP \fIdevice\fP [\fIname\fP]
.sp
\fBzluks\fP \fBclose\fP [\fIname\fP]
.sp
\fBzluks\fP \fBstatus\fP
.sp
\fBzluks\fP \fBlist\fP
.sp
\fBzluks\fP \fBhelp\fP
.SH DESCRIPTION
.sp
\fBzluks\fP manages LUKS (dm\-crypt) volumes that hold ZFS vdevs from within a running ZFSBootMenu image: from the
recovery shell, or from an SSH session when remote access is configured. It uses the same unlock procedure that
ZFSBootMenu runs at start\-up, described in \fI\%zfsbootmenu\-luks(7)\fP, so key scripts,
key files, GnuPG\-encrypted key files, LUKS2 tokens (TPM2, FIDO2 and clevis), YubiKey challenge\-response and
passphrases all work the same way.
.sp
Mappings opened by \fBzluks\fP or by ZFSBootMenu itself are recorded, so that they are closed again before ZFSBootMenu
boots a boot environment. Mappings opened directly with \fBcryptsetup\fP(8) are not recorded and are left alone.
.sp
After unlocking volumes, type \fBexit\fP in the recovery shell to return to ZFSBootMenu, which retries the pool import,
or import pools manually with \fBzpool import\fP\&.
.sp
\fBzluks\fP is only present in images built with LUKS support (the default when \fBcryptsetup\fP is installed on the build
host).
.SH SUBCOMMANDS
.sp
\fBunlock\fP
.INDENT 0.0
.INDENT 3.5
Unlock every LUKS volume selected by the configuration, exactly as ZFSBootMenu does at start\-up: the volumes listed
in \fBzbm.luks\fP, otherwise those in the image\(aqs crypttab, otherwise every LUKS volume on the system. Volumes that are
already open are skipped. This is the default when no subcommand is given.
.UNINDENT
.UNINDENT
.sp
\fBopen\fP \fIdevice\fP [\fIname\fP]
.INDENT 0.0
.INDENT 3.5
Unlock a single LUKS volume. \fIdevice\fP is a path below \fI/dev\fP or a device specification of the form \fBUUID=\fP,
\fBPARTUUID=\fP, \fBLABEL=\fP, \fBPARTLABEL=\fP, \fBID=\fP (\fI/dev/disk/by\-id\fP) or \fBPATH=\fP (\fI/dev/disk/by\-path\fP). A bare
LUKS UUID, or \fBluks\-\fP\fIUUID\fP, is also accepted.
.sp
The mapping is created as \fI/dev/mapper/\fP\fIname\fP\&. When \fIname\fP is omitted, the mapping is called \fBluks\-\fP\fIUUID\fP,
which is also the default name used by systemd\-cryptsetup and dracut. The key file given by \fBzbm.luks_key\fP, if
any, is tried before the volume\(aqs LUKS2 tokens and a passphrase prompt.
.UNINDENT
.UNINDENT
.sp
\fBclose\fP [\fIname\fP]
.INDENT 0.0
.INDENT 3.5
Export every imported pool that has a vdev on a mapping opened by ZFSBootMenu, then close the mapping. Data, special,
log, cache and spare vdevs are recognized, including vdevs on partitions inside a mapping. With \fIname\fP, only that
mapping is closed. A mapping whose pools cannot be exported stays open and is reported.
.UNINDENT
.UNINDENT
.sp
\fBstatus\fP
.INDENT 0.0
.INDENT 3.5
List the mappings opened by ZFSBootMenu: mapping name, LUKS device, whether the mapping is open, and the imported
pools that use it.
.UNINDENT
.UNINDENT
.sp
\fBlist\fP
.INDENT 0.0
.INDENT 3.5
List every LUKS volume on the system with its size and label, whether it is in use (opened by anything), and the
types of LUKS2 tokens in its header (\fBsystemd\-tpm2\fP, \fBsystemd\-fido2\fP, \fBclevis\fP or others).
.UNINDENT
.UNINDENT
.sp
\fBhelp\fP, \fB\-h\fP, \fB\-\-help\fP
.INDENT 0.0
.INDENT 3.5
Print a usage summary.
.UNINDENT
.UNINDENT
.SH ENVIRONMENT VARIABLES
.sp
\fBLUKS_TPM2_TCTI\fP
.INDENT 0.0
.INDENT 3.5
The TPM2 software stack TCTI used for TPM2 and clevis tokens. The default is \fIdevice:/dev/tpmrm0\fP\&.
.UNINDENT
.UNINDENT
.sp
\fBLUKS_NO_TOKEN_PLUGINS\fP
.INDENT 0.0
.INDENT 3.5
When set to any non\-empty value, ignore systemd\(aqs cryptsetup token plugins and use ZFSBootMenu\(aqs own TPM2 and FIDO2
implementations. Useful for diagnosing plugin problems.
.UNINDENT
.UNINDENT
.sp
\fBLUKS_DEFAULT_TRIES\fP
.INDENT 0.0
.INDENT 3.5
Passphrase attempts per round when the crypttab sets no \fBtries=\fP option. The default is 3.
.UNINDENT
.UNINDENT
.sp
\fBZBM_CRYPTTAB\fP
.INDENT 0.0
.INDENT 3.5
The crypttab to read. The default is \fI/etc/zfsbootmenu/crypttab\fP\&.
.UNINDENT
.UNINDENT
.SH FILES
.sp
\fI/etc/zfsbootmenu/crypttab\fP
.INDENT 0.0
.INDENT 3.5
Volumes to unlock, embedded in the image at build time; see
\fI\%zfsbootmenu\-crypttab(5)\fP\&.
.UNINDENT
.UNINDENT
.sp
\fI/etc/zfsbootmenu/gnupg/\fP
.INDENT 0.0
.INDENT 3.5
Public keyring used to decrypt GnuPG\-encrypted key files.
.UNINDENT
.UNINDENT
.sp
\fI/zfsbootmenu/luks\-mappings\fP
.INDENT 0.0
.INDENT 3.5
Mappings opened by ZFSBootMenu: name, device and whether the volume was discovered automatically.
.UNINDENT
.UNINDENT
.sp
\fI/zfsbootmenu/luks\-skipped\fP
.INDENT 0.0
.INDENT 3.5
Volumes the user chose to skip; they are not offered again when ZFSBootMenu retries the pool import.
.UNINDENT
.UNINDENT
.SH EXIT STATUS
.sp
\fB0\fP
.INDENT 0.0
.INDENT 3.5
Successful completion. For \fBunlock\fP, every selected volume was opened, or at least one was opened.
.UNINDENT
.UNINDENT
.sp
\fB1\fP
.INDENT 0.0
.INDENT 3.5
An error occurred: a volume could not be unlocked, a device was not found, a mapping could not be closed,
\fBcryptsetup\fP is not available, or the command line was invalid.
.UNINDENT
.UNINDENT
.SH EXAMPLES
.SS Example 1: Listing LUKS volumes and their tokens
.sp
The following command shows every LUKS volume that ZFSBootMenu can see. The first two volumes hold a mirror and are
locked; the third has a TPM2 token and is already open:
.INDENT 0.0
.INDENT 3.5
.sp
.EX
# zluks list
/dev/sda2 \(dqzfs0\(dq (931.5G)   locked   tokens: systemd\-fido2
/dev/sdb2 \(dqzfs1\(dq (931.5G)   locked   tokens: systemd\-fido2
/dev/nvme0n1p2 (476.9G)     in use   tokens: systemd\-tpm2
.EE
.UNINDENT
.UNINDENT
.SS Example 2: Unlocking all volumes from the recovery shell
.sp
After skipping the passphrase prompt at start\-up, unlock the configured volumes and return to ZFSBootMenu, which
imports the pools:
.INDENT 0.0
.INDENT 3.5
.sp
.EX
# zluks
Unlock LUKS volume /dev/sda2 \(dqzfs0\(dq (931.5G)
Passphrase (leave empty to skip):
# exit
.EE
.UNINDENT
.UNINDENT
.SS Example 3: Unlocking one volume with a chosen mapping name
.sp
Hot spare and cache vdevs are located by the device path recorded in the pool. To make such a vdev available, open its
LUKS volume under the same name the running system uses:
.INDENT 0.0
.INDENT 3.5
.sp
.EX
# zluks open PARTLABEL=spare0 luks\-3f1c6e0a\-5b7d\-4e8b\-9d3e\-2a6c1f0e9b42
# zpool status zroot
.EE
.UNINDENT
.UNINDENT
.SS Example 4: Unlocking over SSH while the console waits
.sp
When ZFSBootMenu waits at a passphrase prompt on the console, an SSH session can unlock the same volume; the console
prompt notices and continues:
.INDENT 0.0
.INDENT 3.5
.sp
.EX
$ ssh \-p 222 root@zbm\-host
# zluks open UUID=0a1b2c3d\-4e5f\-6789\-abcd\-ef0123456789
.EE
.UNINDENT
.UNINDENT
.SS Example 5: Showing and closing mappings
.sp
The following commands show which pools use the mappings opened by ZFSBootMenu, then export the pool \fItank\fP and close
its mapping:
.INDENT 0.0
.INDENT 3.5
.sp
.EX
# zluks status
luks\-0a1b2c3d\-...   /dev/sdc2   open   pools: tank
luks\-9f8e7d6c\-...   /dev/sdd2   open   pools: zroot
# zluks close luks\-0a1b2c3d\-4e5f\-6789\-abcd\-ef0123456789
.EE
.UNINDENT
.UNINDENT
.SH SEE ALSO
.sp
\fI\%zfsbootmenu\-luks(7)\fP, \fI\%zfsbootmenu\-crypttab(5)\fP,
\fI\%zfsbootmenu(7)\fP, \fBcryptsetup\fP(8), \fBsystemd\-cryptenroll\fP(1), \fBzpool\fP(8)
